doc0:Rock and Roll Never Forgets ""Rock and Roll Never Forgets"" is a song written by American singer-songwriter Bob Seger. The song first appeared on Seger's ninth studio album ""Night Moves"" (1976), Seger's first album with the Silver Bullet Band. The song was released in early 1977 as the third and final single from the album. The song peaked at #41 on the Billboard Hot 100, charting less successful then the previous two singles. Nevertheless, ""Rock and Roll Never Forgets"" remains popular with Seger fans, and has become a staple of classic rock radio. According to Seger, he wrote this song
