doc1:Curt Menefee Curt Menefee (born July 22, 1965) is an American sportscaster who is the host of the Fox network's NFL show ""Fox NFL Sunday"". His co-hosts are Jimmy Johnson, Terry Bradshaw, Howie Long, and Michael Strahan. Menefee attended Coe College in Cedar Rapids, Iowa (class of 1987). At Coe, he was a member of the Sigma Nu fraternity, and inducted into the Sigma Nu Hall of Fame in 2016. He gave the commencement speech at Coe College in 2010 and was awarded an honorary doctorate in Journalism. Menefee resides in Los Angeles, California. Menefee called the NFL preseason for
