doc2:White Hot: The Mysterious Murder of Thelma Todd White Hot: The Mysterious Murder of Thelma Todd is a 1991 television film in the biographical film genre, based on the life of Hollywood comedic actress Thelma Todd, whose 1935 death was officially ruled accidental but has always been controversial. The film stars Loni Anderson as Todd, Maryedith Burrell, Robert Davi, Paul Dooley, Linda Kelsey, and John O'Hurley. Working titles for the film were ""The Thelma Todd Story"" and ""Hot Toddy"", Todd's nickname during her career. The film was released by itself, and as a ""double feature"" with another Loni Anderson TV
