doc2:Coen brothers filmography Joel David Coen (born November 29, 1954) and Ethan Jesse Coen (born September 21, 1957), collectively referred to as the Coen brothers, are American filmmakers. Their films span many genres and styles, which they frequently subvert or parody. The brothers write, direct and produce their films jointly. The Coen brothers have been nominated for thirteen Academy Awards together, and individually for one award each, winning Best Original Screenplay for ""Fargo"" and Best Picture, Best Director and Best Adapted Screenplay for ""No Country for Old Men"". The duo also won the Palme d'Or for ""Barton Fink"" (1991) and
